Using file functions in wwbbs.library
---
To access a file database, you must first open the database with the
function:

     APTR OpenFileGroup(BYTE *path,BYTE *name,LONG type)

For the path and name fields, put in the path and name of the file base you
wish to access, prepending the path with "FileBases", and optionally
including a slash.  For the type field, this will be either SHARED_LOCK or
EXCLUSIVE_LOCK, which is defined in one of the dos header files.
SHARED_LOCK means that you only want to read data from the database, while
EXCLUSIVE_LOCK means that you want to read and/or write data from the
database.  You must not try to write to a group that you only have a
SHARED_LOCK on.  The functions returns a pointer to the group which you
will use when calling the other functions.

Some examples:

     If you wish to open the file area "Games" with a shared lock, use:

          APTR group;
          group=OpenFileGroup("FileBases","Games",SHARED_LOCK);

     If you wish to open the file area "Utilities/Disk" with an exclusive
     lock use:

          APTR group;
          group=OpenFileGroup("FileBases/Utilities","Disk",EXCLUSIVE_LOCK);

Just to be on the safe side, you should only open one group at a time in a
program.

After you are done with a database, call the function:

     void CloseFileGroup(APTR group);

For example, "CloseFileGroup(group);".

---

To get the actual directory name on disk of a database, use the function:

     BOOL GetFileGroupDirectory(APTR group,BYTE *buffer,LONG len);

Where group is the group you opened with OpenFileGroup, where buffer is a
buffer you have allocated yourself, and len is the length of that buffer in
characters.

For example,

     {
       APTR group;
       if(group=OpenFileGroup("FileBases","Games",SHARED_LOCK))
         {
           BYTE directory_name[256];
           if(GetFileGroupDirectory(group,directory_name,255))
             printf("directory_name: %s\n",directory_name);
           CloseFileGroup(group);
         }
     }

---

After opening a database, there are four functions you can call to access
the information in the database.  They are tag based:

     ULONG GetFileTags(APTR group,Tag tag,...); /* gets file information */
     ULONG SetFileTags(APTR group,Tag tag,...); /* sets file information */
     ULONG AddFileTags(APTR group,Tag tag,...); /* add a new file record */
     BOOL RemFileTags(APTR group,Tag tag,...); /* removes a file record */

Note that a companion function exists for each of these:

     ULONG GetFile(APTR group,struct TagItem *tags);
     ULONG SetFile(APTR group,struct TagItem *tags);
     ULONG AddFile(APTR group,struct TagItem *tags);
     BOOL RemFile(APTR group,struct TagItem *tags);

Each file record in a database has a unique ID number which is a ULONG.

---

ULONG GetFileTags(APTR group,Tag tag,...); /* gets file information */

GetFile() gets file information.  It returns the number of tags that were
successfully processed.

These are the tags you can use:

     FILTAG_ID
          This tag must be present.  Here you specify the file id number of
          the file you want to get information about.
     FILTAG_Exists
          Use this tag when you want to know whether a file record exists
          for the FILTAG_ID that you specify, and when this is the only tag
          you want to specify.  You must set it to TRUE.
     FILTAG_Name
          Use this tag to get the file name.  Pass a (BYTE **), a pointer
          to a string.  You get a null-terminated string with a maximum of
          32 chars.  The pointer you get back is valid until you call
          CloseFileGroup().
     FILTAG_Uploader
          Use this tag to get the name of the uploader.  Usage is the same
          as FILTAG_Name.
     FILTAG_Size
          Use this tag to get the size of the file in bytes.  Pass a
          pointer to a ULONG.
     FILTAG_Date
          Use this tag to get the upload date of the file.  Pass a (struct
          DateStamp **), a pointer to a pointer of a struct DateStamp.  The
          pointer you get back is valid until you call CloseFileGroup().
     FILTAG_Downloads
          Use this tag to get the number of downloads on the file.  Pass a
          pointer to a UWORD.
     FILTAG_LastDownloadDate
          Use this tag to get the date of the last download on the file.
          Usage is the same as FILTAG_Date.
     FILTAG_Description
          Use this tag to get the description of the file.  Pass a (BYTE
          **), a pointer to a string.  What you get is a pointer to a
          string of the entire description, with lines being separated by
          '\n', and the entire string terminated by a NULL.  You must not
          write to this string, it is READ-ONLY, and it is valid until you
          call CloseFileGroup().  If you get back a NULL, then that means
          there is no description for the file.

---

ULONG SetFileTags(APTR group,Tag tag,...); /* sets file information */

SetFile() sets file information.  It returns the number of tags that were
successfully processed.

These are the tags you can use:

     FILTAG_ID
          This tag must be present.  Here you specify the file id number of
          the file you want to "set".
     FILTAG_ForceSave
          Use this tag when you want to force the system to save the
          current database to file.  Note that whenever a change is made to
          a database file, it is automatically saved to disk, so when you
          use this tag it should be the only one present.  You must set it
          to TRUE.
     FILTAG_DontSave
          Use this tag when you want to postpone saving of the current
          database.  You would want to do this if you are performing
          several changes to a database, and instead of saving after each
          action, it would be better to wait until you are done and then
          "force a save" with FILTAG_ForceSave.  You must set it to TRUE.
     FILTAG_Name
          Use this tag to set the file name of the file.  Pass a
          null-terminated string, maximum 32 chars long.
     FILTAG_Uploader
          Use this tag to set the uploader's name.  Pass a null-terminated
          string, maximum 32 chars long.
     FILTAG_Size
          Use this tag to set the file's size in bytes.  Pass a plain-old
          ULONG.
     FILTAG_Date     
          Use this tag to set the file's upload date.  You should not need
          to use this tag, as the file's upload date is automatically set
          when a file is added with AddFile().  But in case you do, pass a
          (struct DateStamp *), a pointer to a struct DateStamp.
     FILTAG_Downloads     
          Use this tag to set the number of downloads on the file.  Pass a
          UWORD.  You can also pass a ULONG (or any other integer type) as
          long as it's in the range of 0-65535.  Otherwise you will not get
          what you expect.
     FILTAG_LastDownloadDate     
          Use this tag to set the date of the last download of the file.
          Usage is the same as FILTAG_Date.
     FILTAG_Description     
          Use this tag to set the description of the file.  Pass a (BYTE
          *), a null-terminated string.  In that string, you can separate
          lines with a '\n'.

---

ULONG AddFileTags(APTR group,Tag tag,...); /* add a new file record */

AddFile() adds a new file record.  It returns the file id number so you can
make a subsequent call to SetFileTags() and easily pass along the id in
FILTAG_ID.

Note that when a new file record is added, the FILTAG_Date is set to the
current date and everything else is set to NULL.

These are the tags you can use:

     FILTAG_DontSave
          Use this tag when to want to postpone saving of the current
          database.  You would want to do this if you are performing
          several changes to a database, and instead of saving after each
          action, it would be better to wait until you are done and then
          "force a save" with FILTAG_ForceSave.  You must set it to TRUE.

---

BOOL RemFileTags(APTR group,Tag tag,...); /* removes a file record */

RemFile() removes a file record.  It returns either TRUE or FALSE,
depending on whether or not the operation was successful.

These are the tags you can use:

     FILTAG_ID
          This must be present.  Here you specify the file id number.
     FILTAG_DontSave     
          Use this tag when to want to postpone saving of the current
          database.  You would want to do this if you are performing
          several changes to a database, and instead of saving after each
          action, it would be better to wait until you are done and then
          "force a save" with FILTAG_ForceSave.  You must set it to TRUE.

---

There are two more functions that you may find useful.  They are:

ULONG GetNextFile(APTR group,ULONG file_id);
ULONG GetPreviousFile(APTR group,ULONG file_id);

Simply pass any number as file_id, and it will look for the next/previous
file that exists, and it will return its file_id.  The file_id that you
pass does not have to exist.

For example,

     To get the file id that comes after file #10:

          {
            ULONG id;
            id=GetNextFile(group,10);
          }

     To get the id of the first file in the database:

          {
            ULONG id;
            id=GetNextFile(group,0);
          }

     To get the id of the last file in the database:

          {
            ULONG id;
            id=GetPreviousFile(group,~0);
          }

---

Here is an example of how to use these crazy functions:

#include <exec/types.h>
#include <exec/exec.h>
#include <dos/dos.h>
#include <libraries/wwbbs.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>

#include <proto/dos.h>
#include <proto/wwbbs.h>

struct Library *WorldWideBase;

void main()
  {
    if(!(WorldWideBase=OpenLibrary("wwbbs.library",0)))
      exit(0);
    /* open the database `Games/Arcade' */
    {
      APTR group;
      if(group=OpenFileGroup("FileBases/Games","Arcade",EXCLUSIVE_LOCK))
        {
          /* add a file */
          ULONG id;
          if(id=AddFileTags(group,TAG_END))
            {
              /* set its attributes */
              {
                BYTE name[33],uploader[33],*description;
                ULONG size;
                struct DateStamp lastdownloaddate;
                UWORD downloads;
                if(description=AllocVec(1024,MEMF_CLEAR)) /* arbitrary size */
                  {
                    strcpy(name,"idontexist.lha");
                    strcpy(uploader,"Crazy Anonymous Man");
                    size=0;
                    DateStamp(&lastdownloaddate);
                    downloads=0;
                    strcpy(description,"Enter long boring description.");
                    if(SetFileTags(group,FILTAG_ID,id,
                         FILTAG_Name,name,
                         FILTAG_Uploader,uploader,
                         FILTAG_Size,size,
                         FILTAG_LastDownloadDate,&lastdownloaddate,
                         FILTAG_Downloads,downloads,
                         FILTAG_Description,description,
                         TAG_END))
                      {
                        printf("SetFileTags() successful.\n");
                      }
                    else
                      {
                        printf("SetFileTags() failed.\n");
                      }
                    FreeVec(description);
                  }
              }
              /* get its attributes */
              {
                BYTE *name,*uploader,*description;
                ULONG size;
                UWORD downloads;
                struct DateStamp *date,*lastdownloaddate;
                if(GetFileTags(group,FILTAG_ID,id,
                     FILTAG_Name,&name,
                     FILTAG_Uploader,&uploader,
                     FILTAG_Size,&size,
                     FILTAG_Downloads,&downloads,
                     FILTAG_Date,&date,
                     FILTAG_LastDownloadDate,&lastdownloaddate,
                     FILTAG_Description,&description,
                     TAG_END))
                  {
                    printf("Name: %s\n",name);
                    printf("Uploader: %s\n",uploader);
                    /* etc... */
                    printf("Description: %s\n",description);
                  }
                else
                  {
                    printf("GetFile() failed.\n");
                  }
              } 
              /* remove the file */
              if(RemFileTags(group,FILTAG_ID,id,TAG_END))
                printf("RemFileTags() succeeded.\n");
              else
                printf("RemFileTags() failed.\n");
            }  
          else
            printf("AddFileTags() failed.\n");
          CloseFileGroup(group);
        }
      else
        printf("OpenFileGroup() failed.\n");
    }
    CloseLibrary(WorldWideBase);
    exit(0);
  }
 
